From: SaaiOS <os@saaios>
Subject: synaptics td4150: since27 0x1b completes 0x45 chunk

since26: chunk 0 went out, IC answered REPORT_STATUS 0x1b ~195ms later.
write_message waited for TCM command STATUS 0x01, ignored 0x1b, timed
out 3s. skip-0x30 / HELP_SEND_REINIT ran in the middle of HDL.

HDL-v2 / RomBoot handshake: after each 0x45 chunk the IC signals with
0x1b (or STATUS_OK). Host treats that as chunk complete and sends the
next chunk. Do not skip-0x30, do not HELP_SEND_REINIT, do not
touch_reinit while romboot_download_active. need_*=0 after chunk 0 is
not download-finished if chunks remain.

Stock: 0x1b is a report (>= REPORT_IDENTIFY), not a command response.
IDENTIFY 0x10 already completes CMD_ROMBOOT_DOWNLOAD as STATUS_OK.
since27: 0x1b during in-progress 0x45 completes write_message the same
way. Chunk length: stock chunk_space = (PAGE_SIZE-1) 16-aligned = 4080;
SPI write is still xfer+1. Log len as payload space 4080.

Applies after syna-tcm-romboot-hold-irq.patch.

